course: dictionary
lesson: 15987
title: Ute: a word from Australia and New Zealand
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one country. Ute is a word people use mostly in Australia and New Zealand. It is a short word for a small truck or car with an open back, used for carrying things. «The farmer drove his ute across the paddock.» The clues are farmer, drove and paddock, so a ute must be a vehicle that can go over a field.
explain: Look for the clue words around ute. «Dad loaded the feed bags onto the back of the ute.» Bags go on the back, and the back is open, so a ute is built for carrying things. «The builder parked his ute by the new house.» A builder needs something to carry tools and wood, so a ute is useful for work.
explain: Ute is short for «utility vehicle». A utility vehicle is one that is useful for work or jobs. When you meet a word from another place, read the sentence for clues first. If you are still not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: «Ute» means a small truck or car with an open back for carrying things.
fact: «Ute» is short for «utility vehicle».
fact: «Ute» is most common in Australia and New Zealand, especially on farms and building sites.
fact: In the United States, «ute» is rare, and it can be short for a sport utility vehicle (SUV).
fact: The plural of «ute» is «utes».
exercise: «The farmer drove his ute across the paddock.» What is a ute? | A long, narrow boat | *A small truck or car with an open back | A kind of sheep dog | A tall tree on a farm
exercise: «Dad loaded the feed bags onto the back of the ute.» Why would someone put bags on a ute? | To cook dinner | *To carry things | To sleep in | To make the ute go faster
exercise: «The builder parked his ute by the new house.» Find and copy the one word that names a vehicle. | builder | house | parked | *ute
test: Sam from New Zealand says, «The ute is full of fence posts.» What is the ute? | *A small truck or car with an open back | A bag of fence posts | A kind of farm animal | A wooden fence
test: Which word is the plural of ute? | utas | *utes | utees | utis
exam: The maths problem said, «The ute can carry 500 kilograms, so do not overload it.» What does ute mean here? | A shop that sells food | A kind of bag for shopping | *A small truck or car with an open back | A type of heavy weight
